<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tun Perak</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1498">1498</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tun Perak was bendahara (chief minister) of the Malacca Sultanate from about 1456 to 1498, serving four sultans. He led the defence against Siamese invasions and guided the expansion that brought much of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malay-peninsula">Malay Peninsula</a> and eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumatra">Sumatra</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malacca">Malacca</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malay-annals">Malay Annals</a> portray him as the model of a wise and loyal minister.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tun-perak.jpg" alt="Tun Perak" width="320" height="527" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Orhanghazi · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tun_Perak.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
